    "input": "search_document: Yes, you are understanding the rules correctly based on the handbook. Here are the specific details for your questions:\n\n**1. Return Window**\nYou are correct that the standard return window is exactly **30 days from the date of delivery**. This applies to standard items, but please note that **custom-configured bikes or personalized gear** are exceptions and are **non-returnable** [returns].\n\n**2. High-Value Items and Signatures**\nYes, items priced **over $500** require a signature upon delivery [returns].\n\n**3. Missed Deliveries**\nIf you are not present to sign for a high-value item (over $500), the carrier will leave a notice. You have **48 hours** to retrieve the item from the local depot. If you fail to collect it within this timeframe, the item is considered returned, and the return process begins immediately [returns].\n\n**Summary for Planning:**\n*   **Standard Items:** 30-day return window from delivery [returns].\n*   **Custom/Personalized Items:** No returns allowed [returns].\n*   **Items >$500:** Signature required; if missed, you have 48 hours to pick it up from the depot [returns].\n\nSince you mentioned you are not always home during the day, you may want to consider arranging a delivery time or having someone else available to sign for high-value orders to avoid the 48-hour pickup window.",
